# Code Style

- Write TypeScript with explicit domain types for stock quotes, watchlist rows, and notification results.
- Keep validation close to user input and return friendly Traditional Chinese error messages.
- Prefer readable functions over clever abstractions; extract helpers only when behavior is reused or risky.
- Handle external API failures with typed errors and visible UI messages.
- Keep MVP scope tight and document any intentional deferral in `docs/spec.md`.
